-\textbf{Slot hold time.} Full holds the slot for about 51\ms, nearly the entire computation of the four recipients. BIM returns it after their source reads and cuts the hold to 30--34\ms{} (Fig.~\ref{fig:delivery}c). The hold is not shorter still because, although each head reads the source in its first operation, the last recipient must wait for its turn on the shared GPU before that operation runs. The shorter hold lets the next frame enter while private computation continues, which fills the idle gaps of Fig.~\ref{fig:trace}. The dip at 25\Hz{} comes from periodic admission, since after a refused frame the producer waits for its next scheduled arrival.
