-
-\textbf{Deployment.} The prototype runs declared topologies with single-stream stages, and a topology change requires a new plan. A crashed recipient leaves its borrow outstanding and blocks slot reuse, so recovery must confirm that the recipient's GPU work has stopped before its borrow is removed.
+\textbf{Limitations.} Our measurements come from one A100 without MPS, where recipients take turns on the GPU, and from replayed features rather than a ROS~2 stack with its BEV front end. On this 40\,GB card, the 64\MiB{} slot that BIM saves is small beside a 5\,GiB device peak; the saving matters where the GPU shares DRAM with the rest of the system, which we have not measured. The six ordered tests show that stream-only release can serve the wrong frame, not how often it does so under load. The prototype runs declared topologies with single-stream stages; a topology change requires a new plan. A slow recipient holds the slot for everyone, as the late reader did in Section~\ref{sec:eval-mixed}, and a crashed one blocks reuse until recovery confirms that its GPU work has stopped.
 
